MewStage vendor patch allocation/0005 (third_party/NOTICE): Control.ApplyTemplate allocates nothing when no template
is built. The presenter-wiring lambda captured the local `instance`, so the C# compiler allocated its display class
at method entry - 32 B on every call - and Window.PerformLayout calls ApplyTemplate every frame, so every
steady-state UI frame allocated 32 B. The walk moves to WirePresenters, which runs only when a template is built.
Behaviour unchanged.

